Hello,

I'm just scribing to make an enhancement request and drop a translation
file. The translation took about an hour with a friend who were talking
to me in front of me (it was a bit hard I have to say sometimes).

Anyway, I'm attaching the translation file to this message.

I've just noticed that PowerTOP use a cachedir, `/var/cache/powertop'
for me, to store or load a kind of profile. That's a good starting point
because my request is about to save configuration or profile, say
`~/.powertoprc' or `~/.config/powertop/profile' or something like that,
that PowerTOP could load at start up time. That's what it seems to do at
the moment but I have no way to tell PowerTOP to save any nor configure
a somewhat power management profile to fits some needs.

So exposing to the user what the application is just doing plus a
daemon-ish mode to fit an automated usage without starting again and
again by hand.

Thanks,
-tclover.

